From 1c7868c3bf13ace81f479e3dd8fc65d1938d9bdf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 06:45:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Quiet closed CLI stdout pipes at write and shutdown

Four coach incidents were kanban show piped to head or grep -m1, not a
terminal transport failure. A downstream consumer closed stdout while
Python continued printing, then interpreter shutdown retried its buffer.
The sample exit 4 was a subsequent gh auth failure, not the pipe status.

Guard non-TTY CLI text stdout at its write/flush boundary, including the
pre-import version path. Exit nonzero (1), redirect the failed descriptor
to devnull to prevent a second shutdown diagnostic, and restore stdout.
Do not alter SIGPIPE or swallow internal transport BrokenPipeError.
TTY behavior and non-output exceptions retain their existing contracts.
No plugin surface wraps these pre-discovery CLI output boundaries.

Detection gap: buffered exit and early consumer closure were not covered.
Regression tests run actual help/version/kanban-show subprocesses with a
closed reader and isolated home/DB, buffered and unbuffered. Normal-output
prechecks prevent a missing fixture from masquerading as pipe handling.
Unchanged main: 6 failures, 5 controls pass. Patched: 11 pass.
Existing fixes PR2252/2048 address different broken-pipe boundaries.
